userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A maximum matching in a bipartite graph is exactly a maximum flow in the unit-capacity network obtained by adding a source into L and a sink out of R, so each matched pair corresponds to one vertex-disjoint unit-flow path from s to t.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Unit capacities force every s→t path to use a distinct L vertex and a distinct R vertex, so a maximum integral flow is nothing other than a maximum set of non-overlapping edges — a maximum matching.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

